{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's motion commands and perception of obstacles. The specification automata enforce safe, coverage-oriented exploration: forward/random_walk is preferred in clear space, short directed turns are used for obstacle recovery, move_backward is only used after obstacle_front, and full_rotate is reserved for repeated stuck conditions. All transitions are deterministic and only use the allowed events.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion (G1) and perception (G2) to modularize uncontrollable and controllable events.",
    "Specification automata (E1, E2, E3) bind perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforce recovery policies, and prevent unsafe or oscillatory behaviors."
  ],
